course: everyday
lesson: 408
title: Smurfs, cheaters and «infinite coins»
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: Priya's team were beginners, happily losing to other beginners, when one player on the other side started winning every fight in about two seconds. His account was brand new, but he played like someone with three thousand hours. Priya's cousin explained: a very good player had made a fresh account to crush beginners. That is called smurfing. Priya's team reported him. Zara lost to the same kind of player and decided she was terrible at the game, until Priya said: «You lost to someone with three thousand hours. That's like losing a race to a cheetah.»
explain: Theo was tempted to make a second account himself. Then he imagined playing football against the Reception class, scoring forty goals, and walking off feeling like a champion. He laughed out loud, because he would feel like a giant wally. A win you know is unfair does not feel like a win.
explain: Leo's friend sent him a link: «HACK!!! INFINITE COINS!!!» Leo's finger hovered. His dad said that links like that often carry viruses or steal your account, and the «infinite coins» are the bait on the hook. Leo did not click. Ruby's cousin had not been so lucky: he used a cheat, his account was banned, and two years of skins and progress vanished in one afternoon.
explain: Not every brilliant player is a cheater, though. Ollie said «he must be hacking» about everyone who beat him, until Mia showed him a video of one of those players practising the same jump two hundred times. And Noah clicked a «SECRET TRICKS» video that turned out to be just good tips; he practised them and got better the honest way. When Jayden found a glitch that let him win every time, he wondered whether it counted as cheating. His team agreed: if you have to wonder, it probably is. They left it alone and reported it to the game makers, who fixed it a week later.
explain: Other friends met other temptations. Mia's friend offered to «boost» her rank: «Gimme your login and I'll get you to diamond tonight.» Mia said no: it would not be her rank, and she would have to share her password. In Kai's game a player kept flying through walls, which no honest player can do. Kai's squad reported him, and a few days later he was banned.
fact: Smurfing means a strong player using a new account to play against beginners.
fact: Hacks and cheats are programs or tricks that break a game's rules to win.
fact: Links that promise free coins or hacks often carry viruses or steal accounts.
fact: Players caught cheating can have their accounts banned and lose everything on them.
fact: Games have a report button for cheaters and smurfs, and reports are checked.
fact: Many players who seem impossibly good have simply practised for a very long time.
fact: A glitch is a mistake in a game; using it to win in matches is unfair to others.
fact: Game makers want glitches reported so they can fix them.
fact: Letting someone else play on your account means sharing your password, which is unsafe.
fact: Losing to a much stronger player does not mean you are bad at the game.
fact: Real skill comes from practice, not from secret codes.
exercise: What is smurfing? | A strong player using a new account to beat beginners | A player who is painted blue in the game for a special event | A beginner playing against experts | A team that only plays at night
exercise: How did Priya feel when the smurf crushed her team? | Hopeless and confused how he was so good | Proud to have played a famous player on telly | Happy, because they almost won | Bored, because the match was slow
exercise: Why did Theo give up the idea of a second account? | Winning against much weaker players would not feel like winning | His mum would not let him have another password or email | Second accounts cost too much money | He could not think of a name
exercise: Why did Leo's dad say not to click the hack link? | Such links often carry viruses or steal accounts | Hack links make the game far too easy to enjoy any more | The coins would run out by Friday | It was too late in the evening
exercise: What happened to Ruby's cousin after he used a cheat? | His account was banned and he lost two years of progress | He became the top player in the world for a whole month | Nothing, cheats are never noticed | He got extra skins as a reward
exercise: Why was Ollie wrong to call every good player a hacker? | Many good players have just practised a lot | Good players never use the internet at all | Hackers always say out loud that they are hacking | The game shows who is hacking
exercise: Jayden found a glitch that wins every time. What did his team do? | Agreed not to use it and reported it | Used it in every ranked match until it was fixed | Sold the secret to other players | Kept it a secret from the game makers
exercise: What is a good rule when you wonder whether something is cheating? | If you have to wonder, it probably is | If nobody sees you do it, then it is fine | If it is fun, then it is not really cheating | If others do it first, you can do it too
exercise: What did Noah's «secret tricks» video turn out to be? | Just good tips to practise | A cheat that gives infinite lives | A virus that broke his tablet | A video about smurfs and how to spot them
exercise: Zara lost to a smurf. What was wise to think? | One unfair match says nothing about her skill | She is terrible at the game and should quit now | She should make a smurf account too | Everyone else is better than her
exercise: Why did Mia refuse her friend's offer to «boost» her rank? | It would not be her rank and she would have to share her password | Boosting is only allowed on Sundays | Her friend was a worse player | The rank would be too low
exercise: What happened to the player who flew through walls in Kai's game? | He was reported and later banned | He won a special prize for flying the furthest | The game made everyone fly for a week | Nobody could ever report him for it
exercise: Why do hack links promise «infinite coins»? | The coins are bait to make you click | The game makers give them away free to new players | Coins are infinite anyway | It is a reward for good players
exercise: What did Priya say about losing to a three-thousand-hour player? | It is like losing a race to a cheetah | It proves the player is cheating somehow | It means Zara should practise all night | It only happens on bad days
exercise: Which is a kind of courage here? | Saying no to a cheat your friends are using | Clicking a link to see what happens | Calling a good player a hacker loudly | Making a smurf account to get revenge
exercise: How did Leo feel looking at the hack link? | Excited and tempted | Bored and a bit sleepy | Angry at the game makers | Scared of the coins vanishing
test: «bro click this, unlimited V-bucks no joke» | Don't click, it's probably a trap for your account | Click fast before it runs out | Click but only on mum's laptop, so yours stays safe | Send it to everyone first
test: «this guy is level 1 but he's destroyed us 10 times». What's likely going on? | A strong player smurfing on a new account | A level 1 player who is just lucky every round | The game gave him a secret power | He's a robot sent from the game makers
test: «he's SO hacking», Ollie says about a kid who practises every day. Fair? | No, practice can make players that good | Yes, nobody is that good without a hack | Yes, if he wins twice | No, only adults can hack
test: «found a glitch, we win every game now ez». What should the squad do? | Not use it in matches and report it | Use it till it's fixed, then stop using it | Sell it to other squads for lots of V-bucks | Use it only in ranked, where it matters
test: Ruby's cousin: «nah they never catch cheats». What happened to him? | Banned, two years of skins gone | Nothing, he's still cheating today | He got a medal from the game makers | He got all his skins doubled as a prize
test: mate: «gimme ur login, i'll get u to diamond tonight». Best answer? | No, my password stays mine and so does my rank | Yes, diamond is diamond | Yes, but change it next year | Yes, if he promises not to look at anything else
test: «I lost to a smurf, I'm actually trash at this game». What's true? | Losing to a much stronger player says little about you | Yes, you're trash, quit now | Smurfs only ever beat players who are really bad | You should never play again
test: Theo: «second account = free wins, genius». Why's it not genius? | Beating much weaker players isn't really winning | It costs a hundred pounds | The game does not allow two names | It makes your first account slower
test: «SECRET TRICKS THE PROS DON'T WANT YOU TO KNOW» — what's usually inside? | Ordinary tips that work if you practise | A real cheat that never ever gets caught | A way to get free coins | Nothing, the video is empty
test: teacher: «Jayden, why didn't you use the glitch if it wins?» Best answer? | «It wouldn't be fair, so we reported it, miss» | «Because I was too slow» | «I didn't know how to do it, miss, it's too hard» | «We only use it on Fridays»
test: «everyone in my class uses that aim hack». Brave move? | Play fair anyway, even if they laugh | Use it so you don't lose | Report your whole class to the police | Give your password to the best one
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the practice designated «smurfing»? | The use of a new account by an experienced player to compete against novices | The use of an unofficial program to obtain unlimited currency within the game | The abandonment of a match prior to its conclusion | The sharing of an account between siblings
exam: Identify the principal hazard associated with hyperlinks purporting to furnish «unlimited coins» or «hacks». | Such hyperlinks frequently install malicious software or appropriate the account | Such hyperlinks invariably provide the promised coins without any risk to the account | Such hyperlinks are issued exclusively by the game operator | Such hyperlinks merely reduce the speed of the device
exam: Whereas a pupil has discovered an error in a game permitting certain victory, select the response most consistent with the principles of fair play. | The error ought not to be exploited and ought to be reported to the developers | The error ought to be exploited in every match until it is corrected by the developers | The error ought to be disclosed solely to the pupil's own team | The error ought to be offered for sale to other participants
exam: Ascertain the conclusion consistent with the established facts where a novice is defeated by a participant of several thousand hours' experience. | The defeat affords no reliable measure of the novice's ability | The defeat establishes that the novice lacks all ability | The defeat proves that the opponent employed a hack | The defeat obliges the novice to cease playing
